### Lab 05: Authentication Middleware & Protected Routes
### Tested with VS Code REST Client

### 1. Authenticate and obtain JWT
# @name login
POST http://localhost:3000/login/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "israr_lead",
  "password": "secretPass123"
}

### 2. Access Protected /profile/ Without Token (Expect 401: Invalid JWT Token)
GET http://localhost:3000/profile/

### 3. Access Protected /profile/ With Bearer Token
@token = {{login.response.body.jwt_token}}
GET http://localhost:3000/profile/
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4. Fetch Protected /books/ With Bearer Token
GET http://localhost:3000/books/
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5. Add Protected Book with User Identity Captured
POST http://localhost:3000/books/
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "title": "Building Microservices: Designing Fine-Grained Systems",
  "author": "Sam Newman",
  "price": 680,
  "pages": 612
}
